{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775311604,"nonce":"RfIwAsS5mzei1xAEIbu/ISxTLY8=","title":"Watcher restart loses review verdict — coder session stuck in \"reviewing\" forever.","message":"When the watcher is restarted (SIGTERM/SIGHUP) while a review session has just completed:\n1. Review container exits, writes verdict to outbox\n2. Watcher dies before processing the outbox\n3. New watcher starts, sees coder at \"reviewing\" and review at \"waiting:review\"\n4. Watcher doesn't process the stale outbox or transition the coder session\n5. Session stuck permanently — `nightshift revise` rejects \"reviewing\" status\n\n\njessica-ng session 297115a stuck in \"reviewing\" for 10+ minutes. Required manual state.json edit to unstick.\n\n\nThe watcher's orphan detector (`SessionMonitor.check_orphaned_sessions`) already recovers coder sessions stuck in `reviewing` when the review container is not running. But it doesn't check if the review session has a verdict in its outbox or conversation.\n\nAdd: when a coder session is `reviewing` and the review session is `waiting:review` with `completed_at` set and no review container running, process the review outbox and transition the coder session based on the verdict.\n\n- tests/watcher/test_session_monitor.py::test_reviewing_with_completed_review_processes_verdict\n  Assert: coder transitions from reviewing to working (revise) or waiting:review (approve) when review is done\n- tests/watcher/test_session_monitor.py::test_reviewing_with_running_review_not_touched\n  Assert: coder stays in reviewing when review container is still running\n\n- host/watcher/session_monitor.py (modify — add verdict recovery in orphan detector)\n- host/watcher/issue_sync.py (modify — process stale review outbox on recovery)\n\nSee existing orphan detection in session_monitor.py check_orphaned_sessions().\n\nREQ: REQ-019 (graceful shutdown) or REQ-006 (review lifecycle)","files":null}]}